  "info": {
    "name": "Laravel Commerce API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Generated from apps/api/openapi.json. Do not edit by hand - run `make api-docs`.\n\n## Before you start\n\nSet `origin` to the web application's URL, not the API's. The API is not\npublished: it is reached at /api/v1 on the web origin, which proxies to it.\nIn development that is http://localhost:3000 unless WEB_PORT was changed.\n\nPostman needs permission to read cookies programmatically. If requests come\nback 419, allow the origin under Cookies -> Domains allowlist.\n\n## Authentication\n\nHandled by the collection's pre-request script. Send `auth.register` or\n`auth.login` once and every later request is authenticated - the session\ncookie lives in Postman's cookie jar, and CSRF is fetched and attached\nautomatically. There is nothing to copy between requests."
  }
